### Phase 2 — Sepolia Testnet Integration (~3-4 weeks)

**The right minimal contract for your use case:**

```solidity
// ModelRegistry.sol
contract ModelRegistry {
    struct Model {
        string ipfsHash;
        string metadataHash;
        address owner;
        uint256 priceWei;
        uint256 totalPurchases;
    }
    
    struct Purchase {
        address buyer;
        uint256 timestamp;
        uint256 nftTokenId; // links to NFT
    }
    
    mapping(bytes32 => Model) public models;         // modelId => Model
    mapping(address => bytes32[]) public userModels; // wallet => their uploaded models
    mapping(bytes32 => mapping(address => Purchase)) public purchases; // modelId => buyer => Purchase
    
    event ModelRegistered(bytes32 indexed modelId, address indexed owner, string ipfsHash);
    event ModelPurchased(bytes32 indexed modelId, address indexed buyer, uint256 nftTokenId);
    
    function registerModel(bytes32 modelId, string calldata ipfsHash, string calldata metadataHash, uint256 priceWei) external { ... }
    function buyModel(bytes32 modelId) external payable { ... } // transfers ETH to owner, calls NFT mint
    function hasPurchased(bytes32 modelId, address buyer) external view returns (bool) { ... }
}
```

**What moves on-chain:**
- Model registration (IPFS hash + owner wallet + price) → replaces `models_registry.json` + PostgreSQL registry
- Purchase record (buyer wallet + timestamp) → replaces `model_passkeys` table
- NFT mint on purchase → replaces passkey system entirely

**What stays off-chain:**
- The model file itself (stays on IPFS — this is correct, don't put files on-chain)
- Inference calls (stays on backend)
- Frontend routing

**Why Sepolia specifically:**
- Free ETH from faucet
- Same EVM as mainnet — your code ports 1:1
- Alchemy/Infura both support it free tier
- MetaMask works out of the box

**Tech stack for this phase:**
- `ethers.js v6` in your frontend (CDN, no bundler needed — fits your vanilla JS constraint)
- Hardhat for local dev + Sepolia deploy
- OpenZeppelin `ERC721` for the NFT
- Alchemy as your RPC provider

