### Phase 3 — Model Purchase NFT (~2 weeks)

**The NFT is your passkey replacement.** Instead of a random string, ownership proof is an NFT in the buyer's wallet.

```
Buy model → Smart contract verifies ETH payment → 
Mints NFT to buyer wallet → NFT tokenId is the "passkey" →
Backend verifies: does wallet X own NFT tokenId Y for model Z?
```

**NFT metadata (stored as JSON on Pinata):**
```json
{
  "name": "ResNet50 Image Classifier — License #47",
  "description": "Grants 1000 inference calls on model model-abc123",
  "image": "ipfs://Qm...",  
  "attributes": [
    { "trait_type": "Model ID", "value": "model-abc123" },
    { "trait_type": "Total Uses", "value": 1000 },
    { "trait_type": "Purchased At", "value": "2026-04-23" },
    { "trait_type": "Model Owner", "value": "0x742d35..." }
  ]
}
```

**Usage limiting (the interesting part):**
- NFT has `maxUses: 1000` stored on-chain
- Each prediction call → backend calls `contract.recordUse(tokenId)` → increments counter
- When `usedCount >= maxUses` → NFT is "expired", inference is blocked
- This turns the NFT into a **metered license** — very defensible as a product

